## Critical Data Contracts

### Pathogen Profile Keys (`data/pathogens/active_profiles.json`)
```
pathogen_id: str
name: str
category: str                     # "enteric_viral" | "respiratory_viral" | "bacterial" | "fungal" | "bacterial_waterborne" | "enteric_bacterial" | "filovirus"
transmission_routes: list[str]    # subset of: direct_contact, fomite, droplet, hvac_airborne, water_aerosol, food, water, bodily_fluids
shedding_curve_log10: list[float] # 15 entries (day-by-day)
asymptomatic_shedding_log10: list[float]
dose_adjustment: float
dose_response: {model, alpha, beta} | {model, k}  # beta_poisson uses alpha/beta; exponential uses k
illness_probability: {eta, gamma}
recovery_day: int
surface_deposition_fraction: float  # [0.0, 1.0]
base_susceptibility: float
microflora_disruption: {causes_disruption, disruption_type, disruption_magnitude, affected_kingdoms}
introduction_epoch: int
initial_infected: int
initial_time_infected: int  # days post-infection at seeding (≥0); transmission uses 0
```

### Spatial Zone Keys (`data/platforms/*/spatial_layout.json`)
```
id: str, type: str, traffic: str, volume_m3: float (>0), deck: str, display: {x, y}
```

### Airflow Path Keys (`data/platforms/*/air_flow_paths.json`)
```
hvac_zones[]: {id, rooms[], ach}
cross_zone_links[]: {from, to, flow_rate_m3h, is_hvac_ducted, path}
adjacency[]: {from, to, type}
```
**All room/zone references MUST exist in spatial_layout.json.**

### Protocol Keys (`data/config/protocols.json`)
```
protocol_id: str                  # "SOP-001" .. "SOP-010"
trigger: {instrument_class, stoplight_level, min_zones_affected | min_agents_affected}
modifiers: dict                   # physics/behavior overrides (including confinement keys)
costs_per_epoch: {financial_usd, materials: {item: count}, labor_person_hours}
activation_costs: {financial_usd, materials: {item: count}, labor_person_hours}
category: str                     # "intervention" | "surveillance"
```

### Simulation History (`telemetry_buffer/simulation_history.json`)
```
epoch, trigger_status, agents[], spaces{zone: {pathogen_mass, pathogen_mass_by_id, concentration_per_m3, volume_m3}},
summary{susceptible, infected, isolated, recovered, immune, symptomatic, ...},
multi_pathogen{pid: {infected, symptomatic, recovered, co_infected_count}},
contact_tracing{shared_room, droplet, hvac_downstream, fomite_trailing, transmission_events},
reactive_protocols{active_protocols, merged_modifiers, stoplights},
cost_accounting{total_financial_usd, total_labor_hours, ...},
observation_engine{air_sniffer, surface_swab, wastewater_sequencing, clinical_rdt, clinical_qpcr, clinical_microbiology, long_read_verification}
```

### Lab Notebook Records (`telemetry_buffer/artificial_lab_notebook.json`)
Common fields: `sample_id, timestamp_epoch, collection_point_type, collection_zone, assay_type, fidelity_tier, binary_result, inferred_anomaly_score, qc_status`

---

## Coding Conventions

- Python 3.10+ with `from __future__ import annotations`
- Type hints on all function signatures
- `np.random.Generator` (not legacy `np.random.RandomState`)
- Constants: module-level `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`
- Classes: `PascalCase`; functions: `snake_case`
- File paths: `os.path.join()` for cross-platform
- JSON: UTF-8, 2-space indent
- Run `python tools/sanity_checker.py` before committing config changes
- Formal JSON Schemas live in `schemas/` — validate with `check-jsonschema`

## Commands

```bash
python orchestrator.py              # Run simulation
python tools/sanity_checker.py      # Validate configs
streamlit run dashboard.py          # Launch dashboard
run_dashboard.bat                   # Windows launcher (any directory)
./run_dashboard.sh                  # Linux/Mac launcher
```
